cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Measuring Timing Side-Channel Leakage in String Comparison: A Practical Replication in Python"
abstract: >-
  Code, raw results and paper for an educational replication of timing
  side-channel leakage in string comparison in Python. Three comparison
  functions (a hand-written early-exit loop, the built-in == operator and
  hmac.compare_digest) are studied with a leakage characterisation, a
  fixed-vs-random Welch's t-test (TVLA), an end-to-end secret-recovery
  attack and control tests.
